{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9c591def85781bf3", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Vevo2: A Unified and Controllable Framework for Speech and Singing Voice Generation\narXiv: 2508.16332\nAuthors: Xueyao Zhang, Junan Zhang, Yuancheng Wang, Chaoren Wang, Yuanzhe Chen, Dongya Jia, Zhuo Chen, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose two audio tokenizers: a unified music-notation-free prosody tokenizer capable of encoding prosody and melody from speech, singing voice, and even instrumental sounds, and a unified timbre-disentangled content-style tokenizer that models linguistic content, prosody, and style for both speech and singing voice.\n  2. We introduce Vevo2, a unified and controllable framework for both speech and singing voice generation that applies versatile voice synthesis, conversion, and editing tasks by flexibly combining text, prosodic source, and style and timbre references during inference.\n  3. We propose a multi-objective post-training task for controllable voice generation that optimizes both intelligibility and prosody similarity rewards with a GRPO-based algorithm to achieve greater stability and improved overall performance.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-多说话人\n===\nPaper 2603.24589 not found\n===\nPaper 2606.30580 not found", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "7244a64c-3b2d-44d3-8e96-d5bf65e1477f", "uuid": "aa0d2628-48ea-450c-a964-454ea8109139", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T06:42:21.534Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Vevo2: A Unified and Controllable Framework for Speech and Singing Voice Generation\narXiv: 2508.16332\nAuthors: Xueyao Zhang, Junan Zhang, Yuancheng Wang, Chaoren Wang, Yuanzhe Chen, Dongya Jia, Zhuo Chen, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose two audio tokenizers: a unified music-notation-free prosody tokenizer capable of encoding prosody and melody from speech, singing voice, and even instrumental sounds, and a unified timbre-disentangled content-style tokenizer that models linguistic content, prosody, and style for both speech and singing voice.\n  2. We introduce Vevo2, a unified and controllable framework for both speech and singing voice generation that applies versatile voice synthesis, conversion, and editing tasks by flexibly combining text, prosodic source, and style and timbre references during inference.\n  3. We propose a multi-objective post-training task for controllable voice generation that optimizes both intelligibility and prosody similarity rewards with a GRPO-based algorithm to achieve greater stability and improved overall performance.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-多说话人\n===\nPaper 2603.24589 not found\n===\nPaper 2606.30580 not found", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
